  ],
  "text": "The space station is sitting in almost full Earth gravity. Yet everything inside it drifts as if gravity had been switched off. Because those astronauts are not floating. They are falling. So is the station. It has been falling since the day it launched. Newton worked out why with a cannon on a mountain. Fire it harder and the ball simply lands further out. But fire it hard enough and the ground curves away as fast as the ball drops. So it never lands. It just keeps missing the planet. That is orbit. Twenty eight thousand kilometres an hour, one lap every ninety minutes. You feel nothing, because you and the walls and your coffee all fall together. So nothing up there is floating. It is a room falling forever, with people inside. One of these every day. Follow so you do not miss tomorrow.",
  "voice": "802e3bc2b27e49c2995d23ef70e6ac89",
  "model": "s2.1-pro-free"
}
